# Strumming: The Folk Pattern (repertoire plan: st-strum-folk). An original strumming study.
# Your part: G (320003), C (x32010), D (xx0232), G, four bars each, with the same pattern in
# every bar: down on 1, down on 2, up on the and of 2, nothing on 3 (the hand still moves down,
# just above the strings), up on the and of 3, down on 4, up on the and of 4. The up on the and
# of 2 is written as a quarter so the chord rings across the missed beat 3, as it does on a guitar.
# The teacher's bass plays the root on 1 and the fifth on 3, so you hear beat 3 while you miss it.
title: Strumming: The Folk Pattern
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original strumming study
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: strumming, folk pattern, missed strokes, I-IV-V
tempo: 80
time: 4/4
key: G

